    "signature": "fn list_values_row_number(array: &dyn Array) -> Result<arrow::array::ArrayRef>",
    "docs": "If `array` is a list or a map, returns a new array of the same length as it's inner values\nwhere each value is the 1-based index of the sublist it's contained. Example:\n\n`[[1], [2, 3], [4, 5, 6]] =>  [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3]`\n\nOtherwise returns an error",
